# ============================================================
#  Phase 2a vertical slice (design §13): ten events that use every
#  construct of the new event format — classes and tones, size
#  tiers and presets, challenges with partial results and `vs`,
#  spells and the swipe-up option, inline text variation, facts,
#  memories and relations between characters — and teach two
#  spells, Ward and Flame.
# ============================================================

@event slice_ward_lesson
title: The First Ward
class: milestone
tone: warm
actor: thorne
when: met(thorne) and turn >= 3 and spell_level(ward) == 0
weight: 24
art: shield
tags: class study magic
scene: An office lit by one lamp, an old professor holding a pale shell of light between his palms like a soap bubble.
text: Professor Thorne holds up a hand and the lamplight bends around it into a pale shell. "A ward," he says. "{~It stops one blow.|One blow. That's all it ever stops.} Learn it properly or not at all."
> left: Practise until it holds
  grind arcana
  learn_spell ward
  rel thorne +small
  memory: confided thorne
  say: By midnight your shell holds for a full breath. Thorne says "Hm," which from him is a standing ovation.
> right: Ask about the theory first
  lore +small
  mood -tiny
  rel thorne +tiny
  say: He talks for an hour about lattices and intent. You understand perhaps a third of it. "Come back when the third is a half," he says.

@event slice_candle_flame
title: Borrowed Fire
class: milestone
tone: light
actor: lyra
when: met(lyra) and turn >= 4 and spell_level(flame) == 0
weight: 24
art: flame
tags: class magic rival
scene: A crimson-haired student balancing a flame on one fingertip while another student squints at a sputtering candle.
text: Lyra watches you fail to light a candle for the third time. "You're asking it," she says. "Fire doesn't want to be asked. {rel(lyra) >= 12: Here — watch my hand.|Watch, if you can keep up.}"
> left: Watch her hand
  learn_spell flame
  rel lyra +small
  spark lyra +tiny
  learn lyra.prodigy
  say: She doesn't explain. She just does it, slowly, twice. On the third try your candle catches, and so, very briefly, does your sleeve.
> right: Challenge her to teach you properly
  challenge duel vs lyra.arcana:
    win:
      learn_spell flame
      rel lyra +medium
      say: You hold your own long enough that she stops and actually explains. "Fine," she says. "You'll do."
    partial:
      learn_spell flame
      health -small
      say: She wins, and you hit the floor hard enough to feel it tomorrow, but she shows you the trick on the way out, as if it were nothing.
    lose:
      health -small
      mood -small
      say: You end up on the floor with singed eyebrows. Lyra steps over you. "Ask better," she says.

@event slice_stray_cold
title: The Drift
class: incident
tone: eerie
when: turn >= 5
weight: 16
art: snow
tags: mystery danger
scene: A corridor at night where frost spreads across the flagstones toward a student holding a candle.
text: Cold drifts down the corridor like a tide coming in, and the torches lean away from it. {spell_level(ward) > 0: Your ward prickles at your fingertips.|You have nothing to hold it back.}
> left: Run for the stairs
  health -small
  mood -small
  say: You make the stairs with frost in your hair. Behind you, the corridor sighs and is just a corridor again.
> right: Stand and study it
  challenge research adept- wild:
    win:
      lore +medium
      say: It isn't weather. It feels like being looked at, from somewhere far below. You write down everything before your hands warm up, and none of it makes sense yet.
    lose:
      health -medium
      say: You learn exactly one thing, which is how cold cold can be. Sister Amaranth wraps you in four blankets.
> up[ward]: Raise a ward
  mood +small
  say: Your ward flares, pale and steady. The cold breaks against it and slides away, the way a wave gives up on a rock.

@event slice_late_lamps
time: evening night
title: The Last Lamp
class: routine
tone: light
when: turn >= 2
weight: 14
repeat: 6
art: candle
tags: study
scene: The library at closing time, one desk still lit, a cat asleep on an open book.
text: {&The library is emptying.|Rain on the high windows, and the library is emptying early.|Exam fever has filled the library all day; now, finally, it is emptying.} {~Footnote, the library cat, is asleep on the book you need|The book you need is on the top shelf, and the ladder squeaks|Someone has left a half-finished essay on your table, and a biscuit}, and the last lamp is yours if you want it.
> left: Keep the lamp
  grind lore
  say: {~You read until the words swim.|You read until Footnote leaves in protest.|You read until the night porter coughs pointedly.}
> right: Go to bed
  health +small
  say: {~You sleep like a stone. The book will still be there. So, probably, will Footnote.|You fall asleep before your head finds the pillow. You wake up knowing one thing you didn't, somehow.|You sleep well and dream of shelves. The lamp goes to someone who needed it more.}

@event slice_quarrel
title: A Quarrel in the Courtyard
class: routine
tone: tense
actor: kael
when: met(kael) and met(lyra) and turn >= 6 and around(lyra) and around(kael)
weight: 16
art: snow
tags: social rival
scene: Two students facing each other in a snowy courtyard, one breathing frost, the other with sparks at her fingertips.
text: Kael and Lyra are facing each other in the courtyard, and the {season == "winter": snow|grass} between them is half {season == "winter": melted|scorched}, half frozen. "Say it again," Lyra says. Kael doesn't. He just looks at you.
> left: Step between them
  alignment +tiny
  npc_rel lyra kael +small
  rel kael +small
  health -tiny
  memory: protected kael
  say: Lyra's sparks catch your sleeve, Kael's frost puts it out. They both stare at you. The fight, somehow, is over.
> right: Walk past
  npc_rel lyra kael -medium
  rel kael -small
  mood -tiny
  say: Behind you, something cracks: ice, or temper. At dinner they sit at opposite ends of the hall.

@event slice_burned_letter
title: Ashes in the Grate
class: routine
tone: tense
actor: lyra
when: rel(lyra) >= 6 and not knows(lyra.mother)
weight: 18
art: letter
tags: social
scene: A fireplace where the corner of a letter with a black seal is curling into flame.
text: Lyra is feeding a letter into the common-room fire, a corner at a time. Black seal. She doesn't look round. "It says 'well done'," she says. "It doesn't. I'm checking whether it burns better if I pretend."
> left: Sit with her
  learn lyra.mother
  rel lyra +medium
  mood -small
  memory: confided lyra
  say: You watch it burn together. "She's never said it," Lyra says, to the fire. "Not once." You don't say anything, and that seems to be right.
> right: Make a joke
  rel lyra -small
  mood +tiny
  say: She almost smiles. Then she puts the rest of the letter in at once and leaves you with the smoke.

@event slice_hollow_whisper
title: A Voice in the Water
class: story
tone: eerie
when: turn >= 7
weight: 12
art: wave
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A student kneeling at the edge of a still lake at night, their reflection smiling when they are not.
text: At the lakeshore your reflection speaks before you do. "You're running low," it says, kindly. "{mana < 15: I could fill you up.|I could make you stronger.} Just say yes. Saying yes costs nothing."
> left: Say yes
  mana +large
  alignment -medium
  say: Cold pours into you, generous and endless. When you stand, your reflection is a little slower to stand with you.
> right: Walk away
  alignment +small
  mood -small
  say: The reflection's smile stays on the water after you've gone. You don't look back. You can feel it not minding.

@event slice_market_haggle
title: The Spice Stall
class: routine
tone: light
when: turn >= 3
weight: 12
repeat: 8
art: coin
tags: money
scene: A crowded village market stall heaped with jars of glowing spices and a stall-holder with an enormous moustache.
text: The stall-holder in the village market wants thirty crowns for {~a jar of starpepper|a twist of dragon-chilli|a pot of cliff-bee honey}. Mabel swears by it for colds. The stall-holder swears by his prices.
> left: Haggle
  when: gold >= 30
  challenge negotiate journeyman-:
    win:
      gold -small
      health +small
      say: Eight crowns and a compliment on your persistence. Mabel says you've been robbed, but only slightly.
    partial:
      gold -medium
      health +small
      say: Fifteen crowns. He throws in a free sneeze's worth of pepper, which you did not want.
    lose:
      gold -large
      mood -tiny
      say: You pay full price and somehow promise to come back for more. He waves you off like a nephew.
> right: Leave it
  health -tiny
  say: You walk on. You catch a cold the next week, out of spite.

@event slice_wager
title: The Tower Wager
class: routine
tone: light
when: renown >= 3 and turn >= 4
weight: 5
art: dice
tags: social
scene: A knot of students around a table where coins and a pocket watch are being stacked as bets.
text: Half the common room is betting on whether you can climb the clock tower before the bell. Corvin is holding the purse, which is either reassuring or not.
> left: Climb
  vigor +tiny
  chance even:
    renown +large
    say: {~You make it with a heartbeat to spare.|The bell rings as your hand touches the top.} They carry you round the common room on a chair.
  else:
    renown -medium
    say: The bell rings when you're two-thirds up, and the caretaker has to talk you down with a ladder. They'll tell it for years.
> right: Decline politely
  renown -tiny
  say: The crowd groans. Corvin pockets the purse thoughtfully and you decide not to ask.

@event slice_frost_duel
title: Frost Against Fire
class: milestone
tone: tense
actor: kael
when: met(kael) and rel(kael) >= 9 and turn >= 8
weight: 20
art: duel
tags: duel social
scene: A duelling ring at dawn, frost spreading from one side and a faint warmth glowing from the other.
text: Kael asks for a practice duel, which for him is an astonishing number of words. "Not to win," he adds. "I want to see what you do when it's cold."
> left: Duel him straight
  memory: fought kael
  challenge combat vs kael.arcana +1:
    win:
      renown +small
      rel kael +medium
      spark kael +small
      say: You win by a whisker, breathing steam. Kael bows, and his hands, for once, are warm when he shakes yours. Half the duelling club, it turns out, was watching from the doorway.
    partial:
      rel kael +small
      health -small
      say: A draw, of sorts: you're both on the ground. He laughs, a short surprised sound, and helps you up.
    lose:
      health -medium
      rel kael +small
      say: He wins, gently. "You stopped when it got cold," he says. "Don't."
> right: Decline; offer him tea instead
  rel kael +small
  mood +tiny
  say: He thinks about this for a long time. "Tea," he says. It freezes in his cup. You make him another.
> up[flame]: Answer with fire
  rel kael +medium
  spark kael +small
  renown +small
  memory: fought kael
  say: Your flame meets his frost in a column of steam that fills the ring and brings half the corridor running. When it clears, Kael is smiling at you, properly, for the first time.
